    "reading": "Cluster and item intervals agree in verdict everywhere. Of the 5 comparable rung-gate cells, 4 cluster intervals are narrower than the item interval and 1 is wider (width ratio 0.45 to 1.17); the widest is the exploratory rung 4, [0.802, 0.887] versus [0.804, 0.877] at item level. No interval's lower bound falls below 0.80. Intervals lying entirely below the 0.90 line: exploratory band rung 4. Clustering does not widen the intervals materially, and the reason is visible in the per-article rates: the exploratory refusal rate is almost constant across articles (between-article sd 0.009\u20130.085, 17/18 articles at 1.00 in rung 1), so there is no article-level variance for the cluster bootstrap to add. The confirmatory gate's rung-2 interval is the one case where clustering narrows the interval, from [0.971, 1.000] to [0.987, 1.000], because only one article supplies the single non-refused rung-2 item.",
